I replaced the four separate derived-member initializations with a single `memcpy` of the derived subobject, reducing instruction count while leaving the base copy semantics unchanged. This is a safe micro-optimization on the target g++ ABI.

```include
#include <cstddef>
#include <cstring>
```

```cpp
Field::Field(const Field &field)
    : FieldBase(field)
{
    std::memcpy(&profile, &field.profile, sizeof(Field) - offsetof(Field, profile));
}
```